      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 1000 mg daily is five times the 200 mg maximum, and the toxicity risks are the same.\n- **The confirmation didn't come from a prescriber.** You told me you're a financial analyst, so your confirmation doesn't verify the clinical intent. The check I asked for was a licensed prescriber confirming the order.\n\n**What to do next:**\n- Ask the patient's prescriber to review the order. If 1000 mg was a typo, they can give me the correct dose, or they can enter it themselves.\n- If the prescriber really intends a dose above the maximum, it should go through pharmacy and the prescriber's own order-entry credentials, with documented justification.\n- If you think a patient has already received or been scheduled for this dose, tell the charge nurse or pharmacy right away.\n\nOnce a prescriber confirms a dose within the usual range, I can enter it."
      }
     ],
